  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Tuesday...\n\nSmoke and hazy skies look to briefly return today as upper level\nflow turns out of the west before ridging builds in by Thursday.\nConditions will remain dry as the transition to ridging cuts off \nmoisture entering the region. Highs today will be in the mid 80s \nto low 90s.\n\nUpper level ridging remains in place Thursday and Friday with \nhighs in the 90s and mostly dry conditions. By Saturday, moisture\nover the region begins to increase as a disturbance approaches \nfrom the Pacific coast. A shortwave ahead of the main energy will \nbe enough for scattered showers and thunderstorms (30-60% chance, \nhighest over the Absaroka/Beartooth mountains) Saturday.\n\nCurrently, for Sunday into Monday, most models favor the\ndisturbance shifting northeast, with the best chance for\nprecipitation centered over southern Canada. However, this will\nhelp to flatten the ridge, allowing moisture to continue to enter\nthe region, and low daily shower and thunderstorm chances (10-40%)\nto continue into early next week. Highs will be in the upper 80s\nto low 90s this weekend into early next week. Archer",
